<title>MEXICO: Mexico awards Rosarito III plant to ABB, Nissho.</title>
<headline>Mexico awards Rosarito III plant to ABB, Nissho.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-07-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mexico's state-owned Federal Electricity Commission (CFE) said on Sunday that it has awarded the construction contract for the thermoelectrical plant known as Rosarito III to a Swiss-Japanese consortium.</p>
<p>It said the contract had been given to a consortium made up of Asea Brown Boveri AG, and Nissho Iwai Corp.</p>
<p>The CFE said the contract is worth $244 million.</p>
<p>The plant will be located in Tijuana, Baja California and will use natural gas to produce 540 megawatts of power.</p>
<p>The plant will be built in three years, the CFE said in a statement, and is expected to go onstream in 2001.</p>
<p>((-- Robert Kozak, Mexico City newsroom +525 728 9559))</p>
